{
  "title": "Left\u2013right swing-memory asymmetry fails to improve cross-collection Parkinson gait classification",
  "abstract": "Swing-fraction memory asymmetry did not improve Parkinson/control prediction across two public gait collections: external logloss rose 0.043833 and AUC fell from 0.9125 to 0.8917; the joint-bootstrap95% loss-change interval was [-0.01487541408018509, 0.1494605828521292]. Split-window correlations were near zero.",
